From e42dc98e01f6bfd235f81470da3597a8b48f2760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenClaw Hackathon <hackathon@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:08:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(chat): show Cerebras's decode speed as mean tok/s
 per response and session
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Cerebras ends every chat-completions stream with `time_info` next to
`usage`. The completions transport now keeps `time_info.completion_time`
and `usage.completion_tokens` on the assistant message as
`serverGeneration`. Their ratio is the call's decode speed on the server,
without queueing, prefill, network or tool time.

The Control UI shows "<mean> tok/s mean · <p90> p90 (server)", where
the mean and the nearest-rank p90 are taken over per-call rates:
- on each response, over its model calls;
- next to the composer, over the visible session;
- in the working indicator while a run continues, over the calls that
  have finished so far, fed by a `generation` agent event that the Gateway
  emits with each finished call's server timing.
Calls without server timing are left out. Nothing is estimated on the
client.

