From ee32d208ca02e0790547bd0d6e91f6ae53452033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenClaw Hackathon <hackathon@example.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:08:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] docs(dev): example config for Kimi on Cerebras's chat
 completions API

dev/cerebras-kimi/openclaw.json points OpenClaw's built-in Cerebras
provider at https://api.cerebras.ai/v1 with the model
moonshotai-kimi-k3.1-pro-trial and makes it the default model. The README
explains each setting.

The built-in catalog does not list Kimi, so the model is declared. It keeps
the OpenAI-style defaults, which send `reasoning_effort`: Cerebras answers
HTTP 400 to a `thinking` field and to `reasoning_content` on earlier
assistant messages. It offers low, high and max as reasoning efforts;
OpenClaw sends the supported effort at or below the thinking level picked
in the UI. Strict tools are off.

---
